{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "לא יהיה לכהנים", :translit "lo yihyeh la-kohanim", :gloss "There shall not be for the priests"} {:he "כי על פי כהן גדול", :translit "ki al pi kohen gadol", :gloss "for by the mouth of the High Priest"} {:he "על הנשיא", :translit "al ha-nasi", :gloss "upon the prince"} {:he "יהיה העולה והמנחה והנסך", :translit "yihyeh ha-olah ve-ha-minchah ve-ha-nasekh", :gloss "shall be the olah and the minhah and the libation"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Smikhut of parashot: the section of priests adjoins the section of the king"}], :frame {:text "The phrase 'upon the prince shall be the olah, the minhah, and the nesakh' appears in Ezekiel 45:17 and 46:2–4, where the prince (nasi) brings offerings. The comparison of king to priest and Levite in tithing reflects Deuteronomy 18:1–5 in its own context.", :sources ["Ezekiel 45:17" "Ezekiel 46:2" "Deuteronomy 18:1"]}} {:quotes [{:he "אשי ה' ונחלתו", :translit "ashai Hashem ve-nachalato", :gloss "YHWH's fire-offerings and his inheritance"} {:he "וזה יהיה משפט הכהנים", :translit "ve-zeh yihyeh mishpat ha-kohanim", :gloss "And this shall be the priests' due"} {:he "כהנים משלחן גבוה קא זכו", :translit "kohanim mi-shulchan gavo'a ka zekku", :gloss "priests acquire from the Table on High"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Intertextual link: the phrase in our verse is juxtaposed with Deuteronomy 18:3, 'And this shall be the priests' due'"}], :frame {:text "The expression 'from the Table on High' (mi-shulchan gavo'a) for priestly portions echoes the idiom in Hagigah 5b where Resh Lakish states that from the day the Temple was destroyed, a curse was placed upon the Table below, in contrast to the Table on High. The term 'fire-offerings' (ishim) is the standard levitical term for sacrificial portions in Leviticus 2:3, 10; 7:35.", :sources ["Hagigah 5b" "Leviticus 2:3" "Leviticus 7:35"]}} {:quotes [{:he "הלוים", :translit "ha-leviyim", :gloss "the Levites"} {:he "אדנ\"י הוי\"ה", :translit "Adonai Havayah", :gloss "Adonai Havayah"} {:he "ה' הוא נחלתו", :translit "Hashem hu nachalato", :gloss "YHWH is his inheritance"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "הלוים", :b "אדנ\"י הוי\"ה"}], :frame {:text "The declaration 'YHWH is his inheritance' appears in Deuteronomy 18:2, identifying the Levites' portion as God Himself rather than territorial land, echoing Deuteronomy 10:9, 'Therefore Levi has no portion or inheritance with his brothers; YHWH is his inheritance.' The divine names Havayah and Adonai are discussed in rabbinic literature, e.g. Menachot 110a regarding the proper divine name.", :sources ["Deuteronomy 18:2" "Deuteronomy 10:9" "Menachot 110a"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Smikhut of parashot: the section of priests adjoins the section of the king", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "Intertextual link: the phrase in our verse is juxtaposed with Deuteronomy 18:3, 'And this shall be the priests' due'", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :gematria, :a "הלוים", :a-value 91, :b "אדנ\"י הוי\"ה", :b-value 91, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? true}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:37:17.487039343Z", :model "glm-5.2"}